  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following functions has the domain $(-2,0)?$\n\nI. $p:(-2,0)\\to \\{-2,0\\}$\n\nII. $q:(-2,0)\\to (-2,0)$\n\nIII. $r:[-2,0)\\to (0,2)$",
  "worked_solution": "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $(-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (not including $-2$ nor $0$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $(-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (not including $-2$ nor $0$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $[-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (including $-2$ but not including $0$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
